('5a200890-b4e0-52d7-8e7d-294105f800dc'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Table: CP-c24-10 — 75 baseball games: Underdog (Won 10, Lost 35, Total 45); Favorite (Won 25, Lost 5, Total 30); Total (35, 40, 75)]\nThe table shows the results of 75 baseball games played by a certain team, categorized by whether the team was considered the favorite (expected to win) in the game or the underdog (expected to lose). What fraction of the games in which the team was considered the underdog did the team win?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"2/5"},{"key":"B","text":"2/7"},{"key":"C","text":"2/9"},{"key":"D","text":"2/15"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c24-10","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/CP-c24-10.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for CP-c24-10","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c24-10)."'::jsonb),
('692ffc61-2f5e-50a9-819e-bf85276672af'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A tank contains a total of n fish, of which g are guppies. If a fish is selected at random from the tank, what is the probability of selecting a fish that is NOT a guppy?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"(n − g)/(g + n)"},{"key":"B","text":"n/(g + n)"},{"key":"C","text":"1 − g/(n − g)"},{"key":"D","text":"1 − g/n"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c24-11","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c24-11)."'::jsonb),
('3eaf26d8-7e1e-5d85-87f3-c67a2d912dc6'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Table: CP-c24-12 — refrigerator units: Assembly line A (Defective 300, Not defective 5,700, Total 6,000); Assembly line B (500, 3,500, 4,000); Total (800, 9,200, 10,000)]\nA manufacturer uses two assembly lines to produce refrigerator units. The table summarizes the results of a quality control test used to check for defective units. If a refrigerator unit that was checked during this test is selected at random, what is the probability that the unit was produced by assembly line A, given that the unit is defective?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"1/20"},{"key":"B","text":"3/8"},{"key":"C","text":"3/5"},{"key":"D","text":"5/8"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c24-12","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/CP-c24-12.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for CP-c24-12","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c24-12)."'::jsonb),
